# Windows Threat Detection: Initial Access & Sysmon Analysis

##  Project Overview
This repository contains my write-up, technical analysis, and indicators of compromise (IOCs) compiled while completing the
**Windows Threat Detection 1** room on TryHackMe. The core objective of this project was to analyze how attackers gain entry into
Windows environments via common initial access vectors and learn how to hunt for them using advanced logging frameworks.

##  Core Tools & Technologies
*   **Log Management:** Windows Event Viewer, Sysmon (System Monitor)
*   **Analysis Tools:** Command Line Utilities (`strings`, `grep`, `unzip`), Windows GUI Properties
*   **Environments:** Windows Forensic Workstations, Linux Security VMs (AttackBox)

