##  How to Use this Knowledge for Alert Triage
When responding to potential phishing or removable media alerts, my triage checklist based on this lab is:
1. Identify the parent process (Is Explorer or a browser spawning an executable?).
2. Trace the file timeline back to its creation context (Did a `.zip` file precede it?).
3. Check target paths for common evasion directories like `C:\Users\Public\`.

